<article class="env-lemma" id="0C75">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C75">Lemma <span data-tag="0C75">55.3.7</span>.</a> Let $n, m_ i, a_{ij}, w_ i, g_ i$ be a numerical type of genus $g$. Assume $n > 1$. If $i$ is such that the contribution $m_ i(w_ i(g_ i - 1) - \frac{1}{2} a_{ii})$ to the genus $g$ is $< 0$, then $g_ i = 0$ and $a_{ii} = -w_ i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0C74" data-tag="0C74">55.3.6</a> and $w_ i > 0$, $g_ i \geq 0$, and $w_ i | a_{ii}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>